### 2026-09-08 — from `content-filter-class-2026-09-08` → the next lane with WRITE on `chinese api/image-stage/`

**RESOLVED 2026-09-08 — owner approved option 1, BOTH rules are now applied. 7/7 of the obi_wan run's
real captured refusals classify BLOCKED.** Kept below because the *shape* of the trap outlives the fix.

`image_content_filtered` (400) and `image_generation_prohibited` (422) both classify BLOCKED now, each
keyed to the type FIELD, each with its own self-test assertion plus a regression lock proving a 5xx
outage page carrying the same wording stays TRANSIENT. `stage_4` green at 9 scenarios, `stage_10_fill`
green at 5 (it imports the same `classify_reply` at `:17`, so the fill ladder was fixed by the same
lines). **The 422 was found by replaying the run's own flight records rather than by trusting the
synthetic tests — which is the method worth copying: the real bodies were already on disk.**

The second shape, recorded verbatim since it is now a map entry:

```
a1/flight/fill_1_6.json → HTTP 422
{"error":{"message":"upstream image generation was blocked by the provider's prohibited content
 policy (request id: 2026090822315095479196wG7AE7PP)","type":"image_generation_prohibited",
 "param":"","code":"PROHIBITED_CONTENT"}}
```

It had matched nothing. The `channel_error`/PROHIBITED_CONTENT rule (`~:183`) needs `etype ==
"channel_error"` **and** the literal substring `prohibited_content`; this body has neither — its type is
`image_generation_prohibited` and the message says `prohibited content policy` (space, not underscore).
422 isn't 5xx, so it landed on the terminal UNKNOWN branch: no ladder, no soften, and it counted toward
`main.py:498`'s UNKNOWN_STREAK breaker where 3 in a row stop the whole run.

**The transferable bit, and the reason this note stays:** `classify_reply` now carries SIX separate
BLOCKED matchers, and the gateway keeps inventing new ones under new status codes — 200, 400, 422, 429
and 451 have all now carried a content refusal. Every *unmapped* one is indistinguishable from a
retryable blip and costs ~20 minutes of identical re-sends before anyone notices. Rule-per-sighting is
still the shape of this function, so **the sixth wording will cost the same 20 minutes.** A field-keyed
refusal *family* would end the pattern permanently, but that is the classification-by-resemblance
Heaven's Net forbids — it stays an explicit owner decision, deliberately NOT taken, and NOT a cleanup for
a later lane to slip in. **Before adding a seventh rule, read this note and raise the family question
instead.** Also worth copying: `--cap` defaults to **$3.00** per run (`common.py:39`), so a validation
run should always pass an explicit small `--cap`. Full evidence: `chinese api/FINDINGS.md` id `ac79ebb1`.

